[h1]🏛️ Improved ParliamentGraph 3.1 — Proportional Formulas, Historical Chambers & Foreign Parliaments![/h1]

[b]Version 3.1[/b] expands the 3.0 overhaul with live in-game seat apportionment formulas (linked to both seat distribution and historical chamber size), 20+ country-specific historical Upper & Lower chamber names, 5-election rolling seat trends, 3D enameled seat dots, and an on-demand 3-view Foreign AI Parliament Viewer.

[list]
[*]Supported Game Version: [b]1.15.*[/b]
[*]Ironman / Achievement / Multiplayer compatible (zero global variables, zero gameplay alteration, zero background AI ticks)
[*]Mid-save safe — works immediately on existing saves with automatic election data capture
[*]Full native support for [b]all 11 official languages[/b], aligned directly with official Victoria 3 law & concept localization keys
[/list]

[h2]🔥 What's New in 3.1[/h2]

[h3]1. Live In-Game Seat Apportionment Formulas (5 Methods + Smart Auto-Match)[/h3]
Click the new bottom-left [b]Seat Apportionment[/b] dropdown anytime to switch between 5 mathematically exact electoral formulas — or leave it on [b]Auto PR[/b] to adapt automatically to your Distribution of Power law & heritage:
[list]
[*][b]Plurality (FPTP)[/b]: Single-member constituency winner's bonus (auto-matched for British / Anglophone heritage with voting laws). Chamber size: [b]+25%[/b] (local constituency MPs).
[*][b]Sainte-Laguë / Webster[/b]: Odd-divisor highest-average PR (1, 3, 5, 7…) unbiased toward smaller parties (auto-matched for Universal Suffrage under Parliamentary / Council Republics). Chamber size: [b]+10%[/b] (leveling seats).
[*][b]Hare / Hamilton[/b]: Classic largest-remainder quota PR (auto-matched when no voting law is enacted). Chamber size: [b]baseline (100%)[/b].
[*][b]D'Hondt[/b]: Highest-average continental list PR (1, 2, 3, 4…) mildly favoring larger parties and stable coalitions (auto-matched for non-Anglophone Landed / Wealth / Census voting). Chamber size: [b]-5%[/b].
[*][b]5% Threshold PR[/b]: Eliminates splinter factions below 5% (auto-matched for Universal Suffrage under Presidential Republics & Constitutional Monarchies). Chamber size: [b]-15%[/b].
[*]Switching formulas live recalculates real seats, post-formula share percentages, visual dot tiers (100/200/300), and canvas dots across [b]all three views[/b] (Party Structure, Power Structure, and Political Alignment).
[/list]

[h3]2. 20+ Country-Specific Historical Upper & Lower Chamber Names[/h3]
[list]
[*]Power Structure displays the authentic [b]Upper House / Council[/b] with a custom badge, Party Structure displays the elected [b]Lower House[/b], and Political Alignment displays the [b]Whole Legislature[/b] (matching Bicameral Split 1:1):
[*]Great Britain: [b]House of Lords / House of Commons / Parliament[/b] • USA: [b]Senate / House of Representatives / Congress[/b] • France: [b]Chamber of Peers / Chamber of Deputies[/b] (or [b]Senate / National Assembly[/b]) • Germany: [b]Bundesrat / Reichstag[/b] • Prussia & Austria: [b]House of Lords / House of Deputies[/b] • Russia: [b]State Council / State Duma[/b] (or [b]Soviet of Nationalities / Soviet of the Union[/b]) • Qing China: [b]Grand Council / Advisory Council[/b] • Japan: [b]House of Peers / House of Representatives[/b] • Ottoman, Poland (Sejm), Netherlands, Sweden (Riksdag), Norway (Storting), Spain, Italy, Canada, Australia, and Latin America.
[/list]

[h3]3. On-Demand Foreign AI Parliament Viewer, 5-Election Trends & 3D Dots[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Foreign Country Parliament Viewer[/b]: Open any foreign nation's Diplomacy → Politics tab and click [b]Inspect Parliament[/b] to view its [b]Party Structure[/b], [b]Power Structure[/b], and [b]Political Alignment[/b] in its own culturally matched chamber layout (non-party nations seamlessly fall back to Power Structure; zero background AI overhead).
[*][b]5-Election Rolling Seat History[/b]: Hover any Party or Interest Group seat dot to see its recent seat trend across up to 5 elections (e.g. `42 → 51 → 64`).
[*][b]3D Enameled Dot Sheen[/b]: Procedural specular highlight + bevel overlay on every seat dot for sharper visual depth.
[/list]

[h2]🏛️ Core 3.0 Features Included[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]5 Authentic Chamber Architectures + Smart Auto-Matching[/b]: Westminster, Bicameral Split, Commonwealth Horseshoe, Terraced Assembly Hall, and Classic Hemicycle, switchable anytime from the bottom-right popup with rich native tooltips.
[*][b]Dynamic Seat Counts (50–650 Seats)[/b] across 100/200/300 visual tiers, [b]Paradox-Native FancyTooltips[/b] with multi-color stacked parliament bars & 50% electoral majority needle, per-seat hover tooltips, gold coalition halos, Ruler focal seat, and instant updates on government reform.
[/list]

[h2]🔧 Compatibility[/h2]
[list]
[*]Uses lightweight partial GUI override ([b]0_ipg_politics_panel_government_details.gui[/b]) and lowest-priority vanilla-path [b]country_politics_panel.gui[/b] — high compatibility with UI and flavor mods (yields cleanly to foreign-panel mods placed below IPG).
[*]⚠️ [b]Already built into [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3724865565]GORA UI+[/url][/b] — do [b]not[/b] enable this standalone mod alongside GORA UI+.
[*]Playing with [b]Better Politics Mod (BPM 2.5 / 1.15)[/b]? Use [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3697574736]BPM2.5-ParliamentGraph(1.15)[/url] (or [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3726578545]GORA UI+ × BPM Compat[/url] if using GORA UI+).
[/list]

